\begin{lemma}[Antipodal collar obstruction]
\label{lem:ancient-antipodal-collar}
For $a>0$, there is no smooth local diffeomorphism
$F:S^2\times(-a,a)\to\mathbb R^3$ satisfying
$F(-\theta,t)=F(\theta,t)$ everywhere.
\lean{Poincare.Manifold.not_isLocalDiffeomorphOn_antipodal_collar}
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
Compose with radial coordinates on a shell in $\mathbb R^3$. Antipodal
invariance makes the resulting local map even, so its derivative at opposite
points differs by negation. In odd dimension the two nonzero Jacobian
determinants have opposite signs. A path in the connected shell would force a
zero determinant, contradicting local invertibility.
\end{proof}

